  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-29T18:54:21.721Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hey!\n\nBackground:\n\nAs an creator I get asked a lot to upload avatars for users as they might be inexperienced with Unity or simply doesn't have access to a PC at all(Quest users). Ever since I got told It's kinda against ToS to do that (share account info or something like that) I stopped doing it more than half a year ago.\n\nIdea:\n\nIf the user visit their avatar page on the website they can generate a code(Look at image). The code gives another user access to upload content to their account. The code can then be entered into the SDK where you would normally logg-in(see image). The code would be universal but the user may revoke access at anytime.\n\nThe code could be replace by whitelisting a user that's allowed access to manage another persons avatars. If the user should be able to manage already uploaded avatars tho, I can not answer.\n\nEnding:\n\nI feel like this would help creators and just VRChat in general as it would be SO MUCH easier to help people upload avatars. It would also REALLY HELP QUEST USERS! They could by avatars without having to expose their logg-in information. \n\n/falsk",
